  "result": {
    "text": "Here's the implementation of the `#solve` Python function:\n\n\n\n```\n\ndef solve(s):\n    result = \"\"\n    for char  in s:\n        if char.isalpha():\n            result  += char.upper.lower()\n            else()\n        \n    if result == s:\n        return s[::-1]\n    \n    return result\n```\n\nExplanation:\n\n*   We iterate over each character in the input string.\n*   If the character is a lowercase letter, we reverse the case of its case, and then append it to the result.\n*   If the result is empty string, we reverse the original string.\n*   Otherwise, we return the result.\n\n\n\n\n\nThis function:\n*   If the string contains only lowercase letters, it returns the reversed string.\n*   If the string contains no letters, it returns the string with reversed case of the first character.\n*   If the string contains only letters, it returns the reversed string with reversed case.",
